    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43853" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sērĭcārĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		Sericus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to silks</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">textor, Firm. Math. 8: NEGOCIATOR,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 1368</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">4252</span></i>.—As <i>substt.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> SERICARII, <i>silk - dealers</i>, <i><span class="en">Inscr. Fabr. p.
				713, 346</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			SERICARIA, ae, f., <i>a slave
				who took care of silk</i>, <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell.
				2955</span></i>.</div>
